From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:49:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] indexeddb: Make a request's source its object store, index or
 cursor

https://w3c.github.io/IndexedDB/#dom-idbrequest-source is an
(IDBObjectStore or IDBIndex or IDBCursor)?, but IDBRequest kept only an
object store: requests of an index's openCursor() reported the index's
object store, and those of cursor.update() and cursor.delete() the
cursor's effective object store.

IDBRequest::execute_async now takes a RequestSource (an object store,
an index or a cursor, borrowed) and the request keeps it as a traced
SourceHandle. The backend is still addressed by an object store id: the
source's own, the index's, or the cursor's effective object store's.
openCursor() and openKeyCursor() of an index pass the index; update()
and delete() of a cursor pass the cursor ("asynchronously execute a
request with this"); continue(), advance() and continuePrimaryKey()
pass the cursor's source with the request that opening the cursor made.
Values that a request reads are deserialized by the source's object
store (P1.2's key injection), which for an index is its object store.

The IDL attribute takes the spec's union type.

Validation: Host WPT tests/wpt/tests/IndexedDB (4,511 subtests), 8 processes: SpiderMonkey 3,418 (P3.2 tip 3,392), QuickJS 3,398 (P3.2 tip 3,389); the 27 new passes on both engines are idbcursor-request-source (6: index cursors and the cursor's update()/delete()), idbindex-request-source openCursor/openKeyCursor (2) and idbcursor_continue_index "Delete next element, and iterate to it" (1, uses request.source.objectStore), in window, worker and sharedworker; the other differences are whole-test timeouts of the known flaky set (SM idbfactory-origin-isolation, rename-store sharedworker; QuickJS continuePrimaryKey-exception-order sharedworker, plus key_valid.any.worker, 5 of 5 on repeat, and idbindex-rename.any.worker, which times out whenever it runs after its sharedworker variant in one browser, the P3.2 binary too, 2 of 2 pairs each); expectations updated with `./mach update-wpt` from both engines' runs. /_mozilla/IndexedDB/ 172 of 172 on SM. Board results are with the next commit. `./mach build --release` and `--js-engine quickjs` build. These counts predate the P3 review fixes folded into the P3.1 and P3.2 commits, which add a backend test and fork subtests.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implemented the request source union and its call sites, ran the WPT comparisons and updated the expectations)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
